-- title:
--   α-competitive in expectation against an oblivious adversary
-- statement:
--   A randomized online algorithm $(\Omega,\mu,F)$ is **$\alpha$-competitive in expectation** on an instance $(G,c,\mathcal F,\mathrm{cov})$ if
--
--   1. it purchases only elements of the ground set: $F_\omega(s)\subseteq G$;
--   2. it is always feasible: for every valid request list $s$, every outcome $\omega$ and every request $r$ of $s$, some element of $F_\omega(s)$ hits $r$;
--   3. for every valid request list $s$,
--   $$\mathbb E_{\omega\sim\mu}\Big[\sum_{e\in F_\omega(s)}c(e)\Big]\le\alpha\cdot\mathrm{OPT}(s).$$
--
--   The request list is fixed before the coins are drawn and does not depend on them: this is the oblivious adversary of §2.2. Finite request lists stand for the prefixes of an online request sequence, so the guarantee holds at every time step.
-- source:
--   Hathcock, Subramanian, Umboh, Zlatin, Weighted and Unweighted Online Connectivity Augmentation via Geometric Hitting Set (manuscript of Nov. 3, 2026, sha256 e3b9cb64…), §2.2, p.10; Problem 2.4, p.9

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_OnlineCAP_RandOnlineAlg
import Definitions.Def_OnlineCAP_OnlineHSInstance
import Definitions.Def_OnlineCAP_OnlineHSInstance_OPT

namespace OnlineCAP

open MeasureTheory

/-- **α-competitive in expectation against an oblivious adversary.** Hathcock–Subramanian–Umboh–Zlatin, *Weighted and Unweighted Online Connectivity
Augmentation via Geometric Hitting Set*, manuscript of Nov. 3, 2026 (sha256 e3b9cb64…), §2.2, p.10 (PDF p.10):
"An algorithm is α-competitive in expectation if, for any request sequence generated by an
oblivious adversary, E[cost(ALG)] ≤ α · OPT", together with the feasibility requirement of
Problem 2.4, p.9 ("we must maintain an integral hitting set Ht ⊆ U such that Ht ∩ Rt′ ≠ ∅ for every
t′ ≤ t").

`IsCompetitive I A α` says:
1. the algorithm only buys elements of the ground set;
2. on every valid request list and for every outcome of the coins, every request is hit by a
   purchased element;
3. on every valid request list `s`, `E[∑_{e ∈ buy s} c(e)] ≤ α · OPT(s)`.

**Formalization Note.** The request list is quantified outside the expectation and does not
depend on the coins: this is the oblivious adversary. Finite request lists cover every time step
of an infinite request sequence (its prefixes). -/
def IsCompetitive {U Req : Type} (I : OnlineHSInstance U Req) (A : RandOnlineAlg U Req)
    (α : ℝ) : Prop :=
  (∀ ω s, A.buy ω s ⊆ I.G) ∧
  (∀ s, I.Valid s → ∀ ω, ∀ r ∈ s, ∃ e ∈ A.buy ω s, e ∈ I.cov r) ∧
  (∀ s, I.Valid s → ∫ ω, (∑ e ∈ A.buy ω s, I.c e) ∂A.μ ≤ α * I.OPT s)

end OnlineCAP


